tips_time_protect_04=The normal log-on secure time range is from <font color="#3299CC">0</font> to <font color="#3299CC">60 </font>minutes. When the secure time is set as 0, normal log-on will not execute the secure time countdown
tips_time_protect_05=The premium secure time range is from <font color="#3299CC">0</font> to <font color="#3299CC">60 </font>minutes. When an account is online, or has gone offline for less than 5 minutes, <font color="#FFB428">logging on from another MAC address (in other words, logging on from a different computer) will be considered a premium log on. </font>If a premium log-on secure time is less than normal log-on secure time. Then when a premium log-on occurs, the normal log-on secure time will be used up first. If an account needs to be logged on via multiple computers, then please adjust the premium log-on secure time as necessary, or try logging on again after the account has been offline for 5 minutes. <font color="#FFB428">To ensure the security of your account, we recommend that you set the premium secure time to 30 minutes or greater than your normal log-on secure time. To avoid the theft of your account number, avoid sharing your account number with other people. </font>
tips_time_protect_06=<font color="#FFFF00">After inputting a class II password in the command box on the left</font>, click to open the secure time interface
